["2.4","Sundiata","Founder of the Mali Empire who united West African peoples and built its trade-based power."],
["2.4","Timbuktu","Malian city that became a famous center of trans-Saharan trade and Islamic learning."],
["2.5","Neo-Confucianism","Chinese philosophy blending Confucian ethics with Buddhist and Daoist ideas; spread to Korea and Japan."],
["2.5","Ibn Battuta","Muslim scholar and traveler whose writings record the 14th-century Islamic world from a devout point of view."],
["2.5","Marco Polo","Venetian traveler whose account of China sparked European interest in Asia’s wealth and cities."],
["2.5","Margery Kempe","English mystic whose memoir gives a rare firsthand account of a middle-class medieval European woman’s life."],
["2.6","Champa Rice","Fast-ripening rice that spread from Vietnam to China, driving population growth and urbanization."],
["2.6","Bubonic Plague","The Black Death; spread by fleas along trade and Mongol routes, killing a third of Europe and weakening feudalism."],
["2.6","Bananas","Crop that spread to Sub-Saharan Africa, boosting agricultural output and population growth."],
["2.6","Urbanization","Growth of cities driven by expanded agriculture and trade during the era of intensified networks."]
